WEBVTT

00:01.890 --> 00:04.980
I've decided to give you 
a day off to rest, kid.

00:05.300 --> 00:06.840
A rest day?

00:06.840 --> 00:09.960
<i>Come to think of it,
I haven't had a single day off.</i>

00:09.960 --> 00:11.400
But still...

00:11.400 --> 00:14.340
<i>It's not like I have anything else to do!</i>

00:13.990 --> 00:14.260
The Workaholic

00:14.260 --> 00:14.630
The Workaholic

00:14.630 --> 00:14.880
The Workaholic

00:14.880 --> 00:15.260
The Workaholic

00:15.260 --> 00:16.370
The Workaholic

00:16.370 --> 00:20.100
If you're free, why don't you 
help butcher up some monsters?

00:20.450 --> 00:22.370
Butcher monsters?

00:23.790 --> 00:25.620
<b>Rest Day</b>

00:25.620 --> 00:30.560
I <i>do</i> want to get a closer look at monsters. 
It's all about getting experience.

00:30.960 --> 00:33.920
He said the door next to the cafeteria, right?

00:35.230 --> 00:36.700
Pardon me!

00:38.610 --> 00:40.850
Welcome to the butchery.

00:44.560 --> 00:48.810
<b>The Great Cleric</b>

00:45.640 --> 00:48.810
A Salaryman's <b>Path </b>to <b>Surviving Another World</b>

02:12.730 --> 02:15.190
Thanks for coming to help today.

02:15.190 --> 02:17.650
Galba

02:15.190 --> 02:17.650
The name's Galba. Nice to meet you.

02:17.650 --> 02:20.410
<i>He kinda looks familiar...</i>

02:20.780 --> 02:24.290
You can take it easy and chat with me
just like you would my younger brother.

02:24.770 --> 02:25.840
Your brother?

02:29.090 --> 02:29.870
Huh?

02:29.870 --> 02:32.640
Do you mean Gulgar-san?

02:32.640 --> 02:35.240
That's right. He's my kid brother.

02:36.400 --> 02:38.340
Let's get right to the butchering.

02:38.340 --> 02:39.990
You can just watch for now, okay?

02:38.340 --> 02:42.390
#4 Substance X and a Small Change

02:39.990 --> 02:41.050
Sure.

02:42.390 --> 02:43.170
Heave-ho.

02:43.170 --> 02:43.990
That's huge!

02:43.990 --> 02:46.510
I mean, how did you fit a boar in that bag?

02:46.900 --> 02:49.350
Well, it is a magical bag.

02:49.350 --> 02:52.720
Oh! Just what I'd expect from a fantasy!

02:53.110 --> 02:54.920
All right, watch closely now.

02:54.920 --> 02:56.360
O-Okay.

02:56.360 --> 02:58.580
First, skin the beast.

03:00.650 --> 03:03.800
Then split open its belly
and take out its insides.

03:04.770 --> 03:06.160
There. All done.

03:06.160 --> 03:09.060
<i>Hey, that's a lot easier on the eyes.</i>

03:09.580 --> 03:12.250
I didn't realize it could be done so quickly.

03:12.650 --> 03:15.040
Well, I have done it hundreds of times.

03:15.040 --> 03:17.210
<i>There's something scary about that smile...</i>

03:17.790 --> 03:21.180
Do they use all the meat
you butcher in the cafeteria?

03:21.180 --> 03:22.310
Nope.

03:22.730 --> 03:25.840
We sell some meat to other guilds 
and shops in town

03:25.840 --> 03:27.770
to cover the guild's operational costs.

03:27.770 --> 03:31.130
In that case, is my being here an issue?

03:31.130 --> 03:32.480
Don't you worry.

03:32.480 --> 03:35.030
I'd like you to gain butchering experience,

03:35.030 --> 03:38.570
but that isn't the reason Brod sent you here.

03:38.570 --> 03:39.420
Huh?

03:40.090 --> 03:43.820
We get all sorts of monsters
 here at the butchery.

03:44.440 --> 03:47.530
There are many different types, you know.

03:47.950 --> 03:52.410
I think Brod wanted you to develop
an eye for their weak points

03:52.410 --> 03:54.890
and learn the best ways to attack them.

03:54.890 --> 03:58.300
Instructor Brod was thinking of me?

03:58.300 --> 04:03.080
Wait, you're saying he expects
me to fight monsters?!

04:03.080 --> 04:05.760
I'm sure he thought it'd help you survive

04:05.760 --> 04:09.120
when you start going out
on adventures as a healer.

04:10.130 --> 04:12.400
These days, we don't get many newcomers

04:12.400 --> 04:15.020
who are as serious about preparing as you.

04:15.020 --> 04:19.280
In my case, I really just 
don't want to die, you know?

04:19.280 --> 04:21.720
Well, that goes for all adventurers.

04:22.380 --> 04:25.990
But lately, too many are gunning
to become heroes.

04:26.700 --> 04:31.290
They rush out into battle
and are cut down just like that.

04:32.500 --> 04:33.570
But you know what?

04:33.570 --> 04:37.920
Thanks to you, Luciel-kun, the fatality rate 
among new adventurers is down.

04:38.620 --> 04:42.810
For those seriously injured,
the lesson that they aren't special

04:42.810 --> 04:45.470
comes all too late if the wound's too severe.

04:45.870 --> 04:49.180
But you've been saving them, Luciel.

04:49.180 --> 04:53.100
I-I'm very flattered to hear that.

04:53.100 --> 04:57.090
Now then... You see this? 
It's called a horned rabbit.

04:57.090 --> 04:58.500
O-Okay.

04:58.500 --> 05:00.270
Why don't you try butchering it?

05:05.240 --> 05:07.210
Let's start off together, okay?

05:07.210 --> 05:08.260
Okay.

05:08.260 --> 05:10.240
First, split open the belly.

05:11.850 --> 05:14.950
<i>I realize it's dead, but I'm still hesitant.</i>

05:14.950 --> 05:16.090
Luciel-kun.

05:16.850 --> 05:18.420
Just take your time with it.

05:18.420 --> 05:19.630
Galba-san...

05:22.470 --> 05:23.590
Okay.

05:27.930 --> 05:29.690
Next, remove the insides.

05:29.690 --> 05:30.970
A-All right.

05:32.930 --> 05:35.290
<i>The scent of blood filling my nose,</i>

05:35.290 --> 05:37.500
<i>the still-warm flesh,</i>

05:37.500 --> 05:40.150
<i>the feeling of carving fresh, raw meat...</i>

05:42.590 --> 05:46.720
<i>Regardless, this is something 
we need to do to live.</i>

05:48.570 --> 05:51.440
Heya. How was the butchering?

05:51.440 --> 05:55.790
I think I'm much more grateful 
for the food I eat now.

05:55.790 --> 05:57.430
That so, huh?

05:57.830 --> 05:59.320
One thing, Luciel...

05:59.320 --> 06:00.340
Yes?

06:00.340 --> 06:02.500
You should hurry and change out of those.

06:02.500 --> 06:04.610
Huh? Oh...

06:04.610 --> 06:05.710
Oh!

06:07.670 --> 06:09.470
<i>I feel so ashamed.</i>

06:09.470 --> 06:12.540
<i>Didn't I eat meat all the time 
in my last life?</i>

06:12.540 --> 06:16.450
<i>Yet this is how I react when 
I have to do the butchering myself...</i>

06:16.450 --> 06:17.780
Luciel-sama.

06:18.520 --> 06:19.940
Nanaella-san?

06:19.940 --> 06:22.480
Are you... all right?

06:22.480 --> 06:25.140
Y-Yeah, I'm fine.

06:26.290 --> 06:27.440
Are you really?

06:28.020 --> 06:29.640
You look a little pale.

06:31.840 --> 06:34.740
<i>Horned rabbits flashing before my eyes...</i>

06:34.740 --> 06:38.330
I heard that you were butchering today.

06:38.330 --> 06:40.460
Was it actually your first time?

06:40.460 --> 06:45.050
Yeah. I've never seen or done it before.

06:45.440 --> 06:46.770
Is that so?

06:47.170 --> 06:50.240
It must have been very difficult for you.

06:50.900 --> 06:53.350
Your hands feel a little cold.

06:53.350 --> 06:56.450
I was washing them in cold water...

06:56.810 --> 07:02.100
Luciel-sama, you may be more 
exhausted than you realize.

07:02.100 --> 07:04.020
Exhausted?

07:04.470 --> 07:07.480
Sometimes new adventurers are the same way.

07:07.480 --> 07:09.470
They get so excited for their first battle.

07:09.470 --> 07:12.570
But even if they can slay 
monsters without hesitation,

07:12.570 --> 07:17.360
once they're alone,
the mental exhaustion sets in on them.

07:18.060 --> 07:19.910
Is that why you came to see me?

07:19.910 --> 07:21.060
Yes.

07:21.060 --> 07:24.130
Because all of the guild employees,
myself included,

07:24.130 --> 07:26.750
are grateful for what you've 
done for us, Luciel-sama.

07:27.260 --> 07:29.430
I want to do what I can to help you.

07:29.430 --> 07:32.550
Th-Thank you so much.

07:33.410 --> 07:38.290
Then would you mind holding 
my hand just a little longer?

07:38.290 --> 07:39.230
Sure.

07:41.820 --> 07:46.860
<i>My dinner that night was stew made 
from the horned rabbit I'd butchered.</i>

07:47.520 --> 07:48.820
Thanks for the meal.

07:53.210 --> 07:55.470
This is super tasty!

07:55.790 --> 07:56.570
Here.

07:58.580 --> 08:00.540
That again?!

08:02.500 --> 08:06.460
<i>It's nice that I got another rest day, 
but I don't have anything to do.</i>

08:07.170 --> 08:12.280
<i>My magic training has been going
 at a much slower rate lately.</i>

08:12.880 --> 08:16.200
<i>When I gain one level,
it's that much harder to reach the next.</i>

08:16.200 --> 08:18.630
<i>Just like any RPG, I guess.</i>

08:18.630 --> 08:21.430
<i>Still, I wonder if Brod
is busy or something...</i>

08:24.480 --> 08:26.710
Here we go, Luciel-sama!

08:26.710 --> 08:29.470
Nanaella-san? And Melina-san too?

08:29.470 --> 08:30.940
Luciel-kun.

08:31.490 --> 08:33.540
You're lacking in knowledge,

08:33.540 --> 08:37.110
so Brod-san asked us
to give you a little lesson.

08:37.110 --> 08:38.660
Even you, Mernell-san?

08:38.660 --> 08:39.980
So since it's decided...

08:39.980 --> 08:41.120
Let's get going!

08:41.120 --> 08:42.740
Huh? Huh?!

08:42.740 --> 08:47.540
<i>Forget teaching me a lesson! The other
 adventurers will kill me if they see this!</i>

08:51.670 --> 08:54.380
<i>What am I supposed to make of this situation?</i>

08:54.380 --> 08:56.930
I got <i>The Illustrated Monster Encyclopedia</i>,

08:56.930 --> 08:59.090
<i>The Monster Suppression Point Index</i>,

08:59.090 --> 09:03.640
and <i>The Monster Materials
 Armor Crafting Catalog</i> for you.

09:03.640 --> 09:08.060
I brought books about each country's 
laws, religions, and mythologies.

09:08.060 --> 09:12.460
I have <i>Complete Vegetables</i>, 
<i>Complete Mushrooms and Fruits</i>,

09:08.060 --> 09:12.650
Melina

09:12.460 --> 09:14.780
and <i>The Beginner's Guide to Medicine</i>.

09:14.780 --> 09:17.820
Do I really need all of these?

09:17.820 --> 09:18.990
Absolutely!

09:18.990 --> 09:24.690
Hmm. In that case, I'd like to 
start with Mernell-san's books.

09:24.690 --> 09:25.460
Oh my.

09:25.460 --> 09:28.430
In that case, we'll let you 
take over, Nanaella.

09:28.430 --> 09:29.160
Huh?

09:29.160 --> 09:32.880
We never thought you'd pick 
the information that's truly useful.

09:32.880 --> 09:34.540
What was that all about?

09:34.540 --> 09:39.720
Brod-san told us to make sure you gain
more practical, worldly knowledge.

09:39.720 --> 09:42.470
So those two got curious

09:42.470 --> 09:46.300
and wanted to find out what kinds 
of things interest you.

09:46.300 --> 09:48.610
Oh, so that was it.

09:49.330 --> 09:51.790
<i>I'm sure they're teasing me!</i>

09:52.270 --> 09:55.530
Is it really okay for you
to spend all this time on me?

09:55.530 --> 09:58.680
Sure. This is also 
an important part of my job.

10:00.550 --> 10:03.200
Now then, we'll start with a brief overview.

10:03.200 --> 10:08.220
We're in Merratoni, located here
 in the Republic of St. Shurule.

10:03.200 --> 10:11.500
Grandol, Land of Labyrinths

10:03.200 --> 10:11.500
Republic of St. Shurule

10:03.200 --> 10:11.500
Independent City-State of Yenice

10:03.200 --> 10:11.500
<b>Galdardia</b>

10:08.220 --> 10:11.150
St. Shurule manages the Healers' Guild.

10:11.150 --> 10:15.840
At its heart is the Holy City of Shurule, 
home to the castle housing guild headquarters.

10:15.840 --> 10:19.550
Shurule is also the only place
in the world to have abolished slavery.

10:19.550 --> 10:21.700
The only place in the world?!

10:21.700 --> 10:24.520
<i>Does that mean the other
countries have slaves?!</i>

10:24.520 --> 10:27.890
<i>I'm so glad I wound up in this one!</i>

10:27.890 --> 10:30.150
This is the Independent City-State of Yenice.

10:30.150 --> 10:33.470
It's a nation of beastfolk
that many different races call home.

10:33.470 --> 10:37.240
<i>And so, I started studying on my rest days...</i>

10:37.980 --> 10:44.360
<i>Training, treating wounds, study sessions, 
and random errands kept me pretty busy.</i>

10:44.360 --> 10:47.320
<i>Before I knew it, half a year had passed.</i>

10:48.870 --> 10:49.960
It's out!

10:50.310 --> 10:52.870
This month's guild earnings ranking!

10:52.870 --> 10:54.880
Oh? Let's see that.

10:54.880 --> 10:56.340
Yes, let's.

10:56.340 --> 10:58.810
The Lineage of the White Wolf 
is number one again?

10:58.810 --> 11:00.920
Those guys sure work hard.

11:00.920 --> 11:02.510
They're almost A rank. Did you hear?

11:02.510 --> 11:04.980
Didn't we have plans to go eat with them?

11:04.980 --> 11:06.190
Um...

11:07.610 --> 11:10.040
A little space?

11:10.040 --> 11:12.690
Would you mind not getting so close?

11:12.690 --> 11:16.530
Oh, come on! We're just 
bonding with you! Bonding!

11:16.530 --> 11:18.940
Right, Melina? But what a nice body!

11:18.940 --> 11:20.650
Please give him a break!

11:20.650 --> 11:21.910
Hey, wait...

11:22.340 --> 11:25.640
Luciel-kun, it looks like 
your clothes don't fit right.

11:25.640 --> 11:26.480
Huh?

11:32.120 --> 11:34.320
This way, Luciel-sama!

11:35.210 --> 11:37.750
I'm glad Nanaella-san is wearing her uniform.

11:37.750 --> 11:40.760
If she was in street clothes, 
this would totally be a date.

11:41.270 --> 11:45.760
I should say thanks. You didn't 
have to come clothes shopping with me.

11:45.760 --> 11:48.840
If you tell me where to go, 
I can handle it myself.

11:48.840 --> 11:52.020
That won't do. Things have gotten 
a little dangerous recently.

11:52.020 --> 11:53.950
Huh? Dangerous?

11:53.950 --> 11:59.330
Besides, when I first came to Merratoni, 
a lot of people showed me around, too.

11:59.330 --> 12:03.900
Wait, does that mean you were also 
once an adventurer, Nanaella-san?

12:03.900 --> 12:06.460
Oh, who knows?

12:17.830 --> 12:19.380
Thank you so much.

12:19.380 --> 12:20.660
No problem!

12:20.660 --> 12:23.270
I should be okay on clothes for a while now.

12:23.980 --> 12:26.600
You even paid for everything...

12:26.600 --> 12:30.260
It's all right. Brod-san 
gave me money to spend.

12:30.260 --> 12:34.490
<i>I guess this was my first 
shopping trip in another world.</i>

12:34.490 --> 12:36.730
<i>I wonder if I wasted it...</i>

12:38.110 --> 12:40.680
Nanaella-san, please hold these!

12:41.910 --> 12:43.360
<i>That voice just now...</i>

12:49.180 --> 12:50.370
Monika-san!

12:56.540 --> 12:57.920
Monika-san.

12:57.920 --> 12:59.520
Luciel-sama...

13:00.370 --> 13:02.510
I'm so glad you woke up.

13:02.510 --> 13:04.670
Um, what happened?

13:04.670 --> 13:07.470
Monika-san, you were 
on the ground covered in blood.

13:07.820 --> 13:09.920
I cast heal, but it didn't help.

13:09.920 --> 13:13.780
I thought you might be poisoned,
so I cast cure and you finally recovered.

13:14.310 --> 13:17.520
Monika-san, did somebody try to kill you?

13:17.520 --> 13:18.750
What?

13:18.750 --> 13:21.950
This may have been the work of mercenaries.

13:21.950 --> 13:22.900
Mercenaries?

13:23.470 --> 13:26.520
People who will even 
commit murder for a fee.

13:26.520 --> 13:29.190
Who would have the money to pay for that?

13:29.190 --> 13:30.430
Healers.

13:31.410 --> 13:33.430
Do you have an idea who did it?

13:33.430 --> 13:38.280
The other day, a friend of mine 
got treated at a healing clinic.

13:38.280 --> 13:43.420
But they didn't have money to pay the bill,
 so they were sold into slavery.

13:44.630 --> 13:47.760
I thought slavery was illegal here.

13:48.060 --> 13:50.850
It is, but in other countries...

13:50.850 --> 13:52.640
What kind of loophole is that?

13:52.640 --> 13:55.980
Moreover, what kind of treatment
is so expensive you can't pay for it?

13:56.360 --> 14:01.190
I objected to it publicly,
so this may have been retaliation.

14:01.190 --> 14:03.900
So you could be attacked again?!

14:04.890 --> 14:07.550
I can't say for certain that I won't be.

14:08.230 --> 14:12.330
What kind of healer would 
do something like this?

14:13.290 --> 14:16.000
It believe it was Bottaculli-san.

14:16.000 --> 14:17.840
Bottaculli?

14:18.290 --> 14:21.590
He operates the largest
healers' clinic in Merratoni.

14:21.590 --> 14:23.780
<i>So he's some big shot, is he?</i>

14:23.780 --> 14:28.350
<i>Wait, does that mean Monika-san won't
 be safe even at the Healers' Guild?</i>

14:29.510 --> 14:32.480
Nanaella-san, until this all blows over,

14:32.480 --> 14:35.910
might Monika-san stay
at the Adventurers' Guild?

14:35.910 --> 14:37.890
Yes, I believe that would be all right.

14:38.250 --> 14:42.420
But... healers and adventurers 
don't get along!

14:42.420 --> 14:46.500
<i>I wish I'd known that half a year ago!</i>

14:46.500 --> 14:47.820
It'll be okay.

14:47.820 --> 14:53.030
I've been training here every day and
 haven't been confronted even once.

14:53.660 --> 14:57.490
In that case, I very much appreciate the help.

15:01.280 --> 15:04.210
<i>I'm lucky I could save her in time.</i>

15:04.210 --> 15:08.630
<i>I guess lives aren't worth
 much in this world...</i>

15:08.630 --> 15:11.890
<i>But I still have the power to save them.</i>

15:11.890 --> 15:14.170
<i>I have to keep working hard to that end.</i>

15:14.640 --> 15:16.100
Luciel-sama.

15:18.780 --> 15:22.560
I would like to thank you 
for saving me from the brink of death

15:23.230 --> 15:25.020
from the bottom of my heart.

15:25.400 --> 15:27.990
<i>Is it me, or does she look pale?</i>

15:27.990 --> 15:32.120
I-It's okay. I'm glad I could save 
someone who's helped me so much.

15:32.120 --> 15:36.650
Well, as compensation for saving me,

15:37.350 --> 15:39.910
how much do I owe you?

15:41.370 --> 15:43.640
<i>Is </i>that<i> why she's so pale?</i>

15:43.640 --> 15:48.150
<i>Does she think I'm going to demand 
some unreasonable fee for treating her?</i>

15:48.150 --> 15:50.630
<i>Those damn healers...</i>

15:52.370 --> 15:55.420
You've been incredibly kind to me, Monika-san.

15:56.210 --> 15:59.760
So let's just say that you've 
already returned the favor.

15:59.760 --> 16:01.640
I'll consider that the payment.

16:01.640 --> 16:03.080
Huh?

16:03.600 --> 16:08.270
And if that doesn't sound like enough, 
I'll also treat you to a meal here.

16:08.730 --> 16:12.030
Gulgar-san's cooking is really good!

16:12.360 --> 16:14.990
All that must've been scary for you, miss.

16:15.370 --> 16:17.950
Eat this and try to regain your strength.

16:20.850 --> 16:22.910
Thank you so much.

16:24.050 --> 16:25.880
Thank you so, so much!

16:26.540 --> 16:29.930
From the bottom of my heart, 
thank you so very much!

16:30.730 --> 16:35.470
<i>One month after that, the man 
who attacked Monika-san was apprehended.</i>

16:35.470 --> 16:39.980
<i>Of course, no connection between 
him and that healer was uncovered.</i>

16:39.980 --> 16:43.020
<i>We couldn't really say 
the case was resolved, so...</i>

16:43.020 --> 16:45.730
I would like to stay and continue working here

16:45.730 --> 16:49.220
because you adventurers are
 all such wonderful people.

16:49.220 --> 16:50.730
All right!

16:50.730 --> 16:52.900
<i>Things are so peaceful.</i>

16:55.070 --> 16:57.570
<b>Two Months Later</b>

16:57.570 --> 16:58.780
Where's Luciel?!

16:59.390 --> 17:00.490
Instructor Brod?!

17:00.490 --> 17:02.560
Some adventurers are on death's door!

17:02.560 --> 17:03.830
You've gotta help them!

17:05.580 --> 17:08.250
Monsters outflanked them 
at a mine in the southeast.

17:08.250 --> 17:10.670
The adventurers tried to quell them

17:10.670 --> 17:13.380
and managed to finish off some 
of the strange creatures, but...

17:15.070 --> 17:16.480
This is the inn.

17:17.400 --> 17:19.680
You're all right. It's going to be fine.

17:20.130 --> 17:22.810
Damn it! Don't die! Don't die on me!

17:27.630 --> 17:28.610
Luciel!

17:28.940 --> 17:30.190
They're in here.

17:31.540 --> 17:34.390
Bazan and Sekiroth have been poisoned.

17:34.390 --> 17:36.820
Basura is bleeding heavily from a deep wound.

17:36.820 --> 17:40.330
<i>Even if I close a wound with magic, 
I can't replace lost blood.</i>

17:40.330 --> 17:42.250
<i>I've got to stop the bleeding!</i>

17:42.590 --> 17:44.440
I'll treat Basura-san first!

17:45.080 --> 17:46.210
Heal!

17:50.080 --> 17:53.380
Heal! Heal! Heal!

17:53.850 --> 17:55.120
<i>I have to save them!</i>

17:55.120 --> 17:57.340
<i>I have to save them! I have to save them!</i>

17:57.340 --> 17:58.580
Heal!

18:04.910 --> 18:06.990
Next, I'll treat these two—

18:08.480 --> 18:09.650
Are you okay?

18:09.650 --> 18:12.460
It feels like I've spent all my magic.

18:13.670 --> 18:15.860
This is a magical potion to help you recover.

18:15.860 --> 18:16.740
Thanks.

18:19.900 --> 18:21.000
Can you keep going?

18:21.000 --> 18:21.700
Yes!

18:23.580 --> 18:25.670
Cure! Heal!

18:26.040 --> 18:28.010
Cure! Heal!

18:28.270 --> 18:30.390
Cure! Heal!

18:30.390 --> 18:32.070
<i>I can't let them die!</i>

18:32.470 --> 18:34.920
Heal! Heal!

18:42.090 --> 18:44.310
It looks like we're out of the woods.

18:45.340 --> 18:46.960
You did well, Luciel.

19:02.550 --> 19:07.010
<i>I was able to save the three
Lineage of the White Wolf members,</i>

19:07.880 --> 19:10.520
<i>but there were other casualties.</i>

19:11.440 --> 19:15.550
<i>I'm not omnipotent. I already knew that.</i>

19:16.030 --> 19:19.740
<i>But the realization that I couldn't 
save everyone was very painful.</i>

19:20.920 --> 19:25.140
<i>To abate that grief at the very least,
I made a vow to the fallen</i>

19:26.020 --> 19:28.110
<i>that I would work even harder.</i>

19:37.570 --> 19:39.430
Status open!

19:41.200 --> 19:51.160
<b>Skills



Assess Mastery
Monster Luck
Magic Handling IV
Magic Control
Meditation IV
Focus IV
Magic Recovery IV
Life Recovery
Butchery II
Detect Danger II






HP, MP, VIT, DEX, INT, MGI Growth Rate Up II





















Paralysis Resist II
Sleep Resist II 
Charm Resist I 
Enfeeble Resist II 
Silence Resist II
Shock Resist II</b>

19:52.200 --> 19:54.070
<i>It's been a year since I was reincarnated.</i>

19:54.070 --> 19:57.140
<i>These are the results 
of the time I've spent here.</i>

19:55.170 --> 19:57.800
Name: Luciel
Job: Healer III
Age: 16 
Level: 1

19:58.040 --> 20:02.010
There are no performance indicators, 
so I can't tell if this is good or not.

20:02.610 --> 20:04.340
One year, huh?

20:06.200 --> 20:07.200
Okay.

20:11.310 --> 20:14.350
Already? You did say you'd stay a year...

20:14.770 --> 20:19.110
I did, but I don't feel like
 I've progressed much yet.

20:19.110 --> 20:21.650
Relax. You're definitely improving.

20:21.650 --> 20:26.720
I still can't read your attacks, 
and I still can't hit you with mine.

20:26.720 --> 20:29.620
Plus, my only spells are heal and cure.

20:29.620 --> 20:33.440
You and I have very different 
experience levels and statuses.

20:33.440 --> 20:36.770
If you had managed to hit me, 
I'd be in bed for days from the shock.

20:36.770 --> 20:38.340
<i>We're </i>that<i> far apart?</i>

20:41.830 --> 20:45.680
It's only been a year,
but I trained to the best of my ability.

20:46.630 --> 20:47.860
Instructor Brod.

20:48.470 --> 20:51.770
Thank you very much for the past year!

20:52.330 --> 20:56.060
Now if I run into any monsters, 
I'm confident that I can run away!

20:56.060 --> 20:58.810
Hey, don't you mean "take them down"?

20:58.810 --> 21:02.420
Why don't you just get a job 
at the Adventurers' Guild?

21:02.420 --> 21:05.490
See? Even Monika's working
here as a receptionist.

21:05.490 --> 21:10.320
Well, I kind of want to earn money 
and learn new magic, so...

21:10.320 --> 21:12.330
Yeah, I guess you would.

21:12.810 --> 21:16.150
Also, I think that if I can learn new magic,

21:16.150 --> 21:19.170
I may be able to save a few more lives.

21:19.680 --> 21:21.560
It sounds like you've made up your mind.

21:22.240 --> 21:24.490
Well then, what will you do now?

21:24.490 --> 21:29.360
I'll get a referral to a healing clinic
and save up money to buy a spell tome.

21:29.360 --> 21:33.220
I plan to stay based here in town, 
so I'll come back to train again.

21:33.220 --> 21:36.040
I'll also accept healing requests 
for a very low fee.

21:36.040 --> 21:37.940
And after you buy a spell tome?

21:39.840 --> 21:45.030
Work until I've mastered it, 
 then earn money with that

21:45.570 --> 21:49.870
so I can eventually start a clinic
that's easy on everyone's wallet.

21:50.930 --> 21:53.330
Yeah. Sounds just like you, Luciel.

21:56.190 --> 21:58.540
It's been a very enjoyable year.

21:58.540 --> 22:00.920
It has been, Instructor Brod.

22:01.440 --> 22:02.550
I feel the same way.

22:03.480 --> 22:06.880
I really owe everything to you.

22:19.070 --> 22:20.130
All right.

22:21.780 --> 22:23.650
On to another bright day!

23:55.620 --> 23:58.300
Luciel-kun really is a good, sincere kid.

23:58.300 --> 24:00.930
I can understand what Brod saw in him.

24:00.930 --> 24:03.580
There's a lot I'd also like to teach him.

24:03.580 --> 24:06.120
Next time: "The Healing Clinic 
and the Arrival of Bottaculli."

24:06.250 --> 24:09.960
#5 The Healing Clinic and the Arrival of Bottaculli

24:07.060 --> 24:09.580
Animals aren't the only creatures 
to butcher, you know.
